The tests all call the same helper repeatedly in one process, and that helper never resets module state. In `_language_extensions.py`, `_ACCOUNT_ID` is a module-global initialized to `None`. For `_FIM_OBJ = ["MyMap", {"Ref": "AWS::AccountId"}, "v"]`, `_ForEachValueFnFindInMap.value` reaches the `if mapping:` block and first evaluates `t_map[1].value(...)`. `_ForEachValueRef.value` handles `AWS::AccountId` by raising if `_ACCOUNT_ID is None`, but returning `_ACCOUNT_ID` once it has been set. On the first call, that raise sends control into the fallback loop in `_ForEachValueFnFindInMap.value`, where a matching mapping key can be written back into `_ACCOUNT_ID`. On later calls, the same `Ref` resolves immediately, so the fallback loop is skipped and execution goes straight to the final lookup/return path. Because the first call and later calls take different branches inside `_ForEachValueFnFindInMap.value`, the per-call executed line-number sequences are not all identical.

